{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The section <b>And it came to pass in the fourteenth year</b> is explained in the book of Kings. If there are additional words, the meanings are equivalent, for the additional words—their meanings are equivalent, for the words are as vessels and the meanings are as what fills them. Now I shall explain that there are [should be: six] words:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "The text repeats 'הטעמים הם שוים' and the phrase 'המלות ככלים והטעמים הם כפועלים' is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The marginal note צ\"ל שש indicates the intended number is 'six.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:47.864687042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}